Subject: Compare IgnoreList rules instead of setuptools matchers

Setuptools 83 introduced Unicode-normalising matcher wrappers without
value-based equality. Comparing independently constructed IgnoreList
instances therefore fails even when their rules are identical.

Record the glob patterns separately for equality and diagnostics while
retaining setuptools' matchers for filtering. Keep both lists in sync
when adding, clearing or combining rules. Add regression tests, including
opaque matchers that reproduce the failure with older setuptools too.
